 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was met: five settings on five different scenes failed in every repeat (S1, S9, S20, S33, S37). All of them combine the fastest ego speed at hand-off (1.4x) with the slowest retimed car (0.5x). Only the timing of the car differs, from 2 s early to 1 s late. Each setting has only a few repeats, so its 90% range only just clears 0.5. These settings are confirmed as failing, but how often each one fails is not pinned down. Only two of the five are clearly the policy's fault: S9 and S37, where it drifted left into a car in the next lane. At S20 and S33 the faster replayed ego had already closed to a few metres behind a slower lead car before hand-off, with about 0.5 s left. Those failures may come from the setup rather than the policy. S1 is mixed.",
